0000:                   ********************************************************************
0000:                   * SCF - NitrOS-9 Sequential Character File Manager
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * This contains an added SetStat call to allow placing prearranged data
0000:                   * into the keyboard buffer of ANY SCF related device.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Usage:
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Entry: X = Pointer to the string
0000:                   *        Y = Length of the string
0000:                   *        A = Path number
0000:                   *        B = SS.Fill ($A0) (syscall SETSTAT function call number)
0000:                   * NOTE: If high bit of Y is set, no carriage return will be appended to
0000:                   *       the read buffer (used in Shellplus V2.2 history)
0000:                   *
0000:                   * This also includes Kevin Darlings SCF Editor patches.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *          1993/04/20  ???
0000:                   * V1.09:
0000:                   * - Speeded up L05CC (write char to device) routine by a few cycles
0000:                   * - Slightly optimized Insert char.
0000:                   * - Move branch table so Read & ReadLn are 1 cycle faster each; fixed
0000:                   *   SS.Fill so size is truncated @ 256 bytes.
0000:                   * - Added NO CR option to SS.Fill (for use with modified Shellplus V2.2
0000:                   *   command history).
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/04/21  ???
0000:                   * Slight speedup to some of ReadLn parsing, TFM's in Open/Close.
0000:                   * - More optimization to read/write driver calls
0000:                   * - Got rid of branch table @ L05E3 for speed
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/05/21  ???
0000:                   * V1.10:
0000:                   * Added Boisy Pitre's patch for non-sharable devices.
0000:                   * - Saved 4 cycles in routine @ L042B
0000:                   * - Modified Boisy's routine to not pshs/puls B (saves 2 cycles).
0000:                   * - Changed buffer prefill of CR's to save 1 byte.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/07/27  ???
0000:                   * V1.11:
0000:                   * Changed a BRA to a LBRA to a straight LBRA in L0322.
0000:                   * - Optimized path option character routine @ L032C
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/08/03  ???
0000:                   * Modified vector table @ L033F to save 1 cycle on PD.PSC
0000:                   * - Sped up uppercase conversion checks for ReadLn & WritLn
0000:                   * - Changed 2 BRA's to L02F9 to do an LBRA straight to L05F8 (ReadLn loop)
0000:                   * - Moved L0565 routine so Reprint line, Insert & Delete char (on ReadLn)
0000:                   *   are 1 cycle faster / char printed
0000:                   * - Changed 2 references to L0420 to go straight to L0565
0000:                   * - Sped up ReadLn loop by 2 or 3 cycles per char read
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/09/21  ???
0000:                   * V1.12:
0000:                   * Sped up L0435 by 1 or 2 cycles (depending on branch)
0000:                   * - Changed LDD ,S to TFR X,D (saves 1 cycle) @ L04F1 (Write & WritLn)
0000:                   * - Modified L04F1 to use W without TFR (+1 byte, -3 cycles) (Write)
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/11/09  ???
0000:                   * Took LDX #0/LDU PD.BUF,y from L03B5 & merged in @ L028A, L02EF & L0381.
0000:                   * Also changed BEQ @ L03A5 to skip re-loading X with 0.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/11/10  ???
0000:                   * Moved L04B2 routine to allow a couple of BSR's instead of LBSR's In READ.
0000:                   * - Moved driver call right into READ loop (should save 25 cycles/char read)
0000:                   * - Moved driver call right into L0565 (should save 12 cycles/char written on echo,
0000:                   *   line editing, etc.)
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/11/26  ???
0000:                   * Moved L02FE (ReadLn parsing) to end where ReadLn routine is moved L03E2
0000:                   * so Read loop would be optimized for it (read char from driver) instead of
0000:                   * L042B (write filled buffer to caller).
0000:                   * Changed LDA #C$NULL to CLRA.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1993/12/01  ???
0000:                   * Modified device write call (L056F) to preserve Y as well, to cut down on
0000:                   * PSHS/PULS.
0000:                   * - Changed L03E2 & L03DA to exit immediately if PD.DEV or PD.DV2 (depending
0000:                   * on which routine) is empty (eliminated redundant LEAX ,X).
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/05/31  ???
0000:                   * Attempted mode to L03F1 to eliminate LDW #D$READ, changed:
0000:                   *      LDX V$DRIV,x
0000:                   *      ADDW M$Exec,x
0000:                   *      JSR w,x
0000:                   * to:
0000:                   *      LDW V$DRIV,x
0000:                   *      ADDW M$Exec,w
0000:                   *      JSR D$READ,w
0000:                   * Did same to L05C9 & L056F (should speed up each by 1 cycle)
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/06/07  ???
0000:                   * Attempted to modify all M$Exec calls to use new V$DRIVEX (REQUIRES NEW IOMAN)
0000:                   * - L01FA (Get/SetStat), L03F1 (Read), L05C9 (Write), L056F (Write)
0000:                   * - Changed L046A to use LDB V.BUSY,x...CMPB ,s...TFR B,A
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/06/08  ???
0000:                   * Changed TST <PD.EKO,y in read loop (L02BC) to LDB PD.EKO,y
0000:                   * - Changed LEAX 1,X to LDB #1/ABX @ L02C4
0000:                   * - Changed LEAX >L033F,pc @ L032C to use < (8 bit) version
0000:                   * - Modified L02E5 to use D instead of X, allowing TSTA, and faster exit on 0 byte
0000:                   *   just BRAnching to L0453
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/06/09  ???
0000:                   * Changed LEAX 1,X to LDB #1/ABX @ L053D, L05F8, L0312, L0351, L03B8
0000:                   * - Changed to L0573: All TST's changed to LDB's
0000:                   * - Changed Open/Create init to use LEAX,PC instead of BSR/PULS X
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.CNT,y to LDA PD.CNT,y @ close
0000:                   * - Eliminated L010D, changed references to it to go to L0129
0000:                   * - Eliminated useless LEAX ,X @ L0182, and changed BEQ @ L0182 to go to L012A
0000:                   *   instead of L0129 (speeds CLOSE by 5 or 10 cycles)
0000:                   * - Moved L06B9 into L012B, eliminate BSR/RTS, plus
0000:                   * - Changed TST V.TYPE,x to LDB V.TYPE,x
0000:                   * - Moved L0624 to just before L05F8 to eliminate BRA L05F8 (ReadLn)
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.EKO,y @ L0413 to LDB PD.EKO,y
0000:                   * - Moved L0413-L0423 routines to later in code to allow short branches
0000:                   * - As result of above, changed 6 LBxx to Bxx
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.MIN,y @ L04BB to LDA PD.MIN,y
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.RAW,y/TST PD.UPC,y @ L0523 to LDB's
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.ALF,y @ L052A to LDB
0000:                   * - L053D: Moved TST PD.RAW,y to before LDA -1,u to speed up WRITE, changed it to LDB
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/06/10  ???
0000:                   * Changed TST PD.ALF,y to LDB @ L052A
0000:                   * - Changed CLR V.WAKE,u to CLRA/STA V.WAKE,u @ L03F1 (Read)
0000:                   * - Changed CLR V.BUSY,u to CLRA/STA V.BUSY,u @ L045D
0000:                   * - Changed CLR PD.MIN,y to CLRA/STA PD.MIN,y, moved before LDA P$ID,x @ L04A7
0000:                   * - Changed CLR PD.RAW,y @ L04BB to STA PD.RAW, since A already 0 to get there
0000:                   * - Changed CLR V.PAUS,u to CLRA/STA V.PAUS,u @ L05A2
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.RAW,y to LDA PD.RAW,y @ L05A2
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.ALF,y to LDA PD.ALF,y @ L05A2
0000:                   * - Changed CLR V.WAKE,u to CLRB/STB V.WAKE,u @ L05C9
0000:                   * - Changed CLR V.WAKE,u to CLRB/STB V.WAKE,u @ L056F
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.UPC,y to LDB PD.UPC,y @ L0322
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.DLO,y/TST PD.EKO,y to LDB's @ L03A5
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          1994/06/16  ???
0000:                   * Changed TST PD.UPC,y to LDB PD.UPC,y @ L0322
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.BSO,y to LDB PD.BSO,y @ L03BF
0000:                   * - Changed TST PD.EKO,y to LDB PD.EKO,y @ L03BF
0000:                   *
0000:                   *          2002/10/11  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Merged NitrOS-9 and TuneUp versions for single-source maintenance.  Note that
0000:                   * the 6809 version of TuneUp never seemed to call GrfDrv directly to do fast screen
0000:                   * writes (see note around g.done label).
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  16r2    2002/05/16  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Removed pshs/puls of b from sharable code segment for non-NitrOS-9 because it was
0000:                   * not needed.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  16r3    2002/08/16  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Now uses V$DRIVEX.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  16r4    2004/07/12  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * 6809 version now calls the FAST TEXT entry point of GrfDrv.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  17      2010/01/15  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Fix for bug described in Artifact 2932883 on SF
0000:                   * Also added Level 1 conditionals for eventual backporting
0000:                   
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  17      2010/01/15  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Handling of device exclusivity using the SHARE. bit has been rearchitected.
0000:                   * The '93 patch looked at the mode bytes in the descriptor and driver and
0000:                   * determined that if both were set, then only one path would be allowed to
0000:                   * be opened on the device at a time.
0000:                   * I now believe this is wrong.
0000:                   * The mode bytes in the device driver and descriptor are capability bytes.
0000:                   * They advertise what the device is capable of doing (READ, WRITE, etc) so
0000:                   * the mode bytes alone do not convey action, but merely what is possible.
0000:                   * When the user calls I$Open on a device, he passes the desired mode byte
0000:                   * in RegA and IOMan checks to make sure that all bits in that register are
0000:                   * set in the mode bytes of the driver and descriptor.  So once we get into
0000:                   * the Open call of this file manager, we know that all set bits in RegA are
0000:                   * also set in the mode bytes of the driver and descriptor.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * For SHARE., what we SHOULD be doing is checking the number of open paths
0000:                   * on the device.  If the SHARE. bit is set in RegA, then we check if a path
0000:                   * is already open and if so, return the E$DevBsy error.
0000:                   * Likewise, if SHARE. is not set in RegA, we check the path at the head of
0000:                   * the open path list, and if ITS mode byte has the SHARE. bit set, we exit
0000:                   * with E$DevBsy too.  The idea is that if the SHARE. bit is set on the newly
0000:                   * opened path or an existing path, then there can "be only one."
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  18      2010/01/23  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * SCF has successfully been backported to NitrOS-9 Level 1.
0000:                   * SCF now returns on carry set after calling SS.Open.  Prior to this
0000:                   * change, SS.ComSt would be called right after SS.Open even if SS.Open
0000:                   * failed. This caused misery with the scdwn driver wildcard feature.
0000:                   *
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   SCF
0000:                            ttl   NitrOS-9 Sequential Character File Manager
0000:                   
