071F:                   ********************************************************************
071F:                   * KANJI extension (Japanese text editing in ReadLn)
071F:                   *
071F:                   * The path descriptor option PD.PAR (unused by the SCF drivers of the
071F:                   * simulator) selects the character encoding of the terminal:
071F:                   *   0 = single byte (original behaviour)   1 = UTF-8
071F:                   *   2 = EUC-JP                             3 = Shift_JIS (CP932)
071F:                   * In these modes a backspace removes one whole character from the line
071F:                   * buffer and the erase sequence (BSE or BSE,SP,BSE) is echoed once for
071F:                   * every display column the character occupies (2 for full width kanji
071F:                   * and kana, 1 for ASCII and half width katakana).
071F:                   *
071F:                   * Entry: X = character count (> 0), U = buffer pointer, Y = path descriptor
071F:                   * Exit : X, U moved back over the last character
071F: 3084              KBsp     leax  ,x           Any characters?
